        "1TI.3.10"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "Additionally, they must first be tested. Then, if they are above reproach, let them serve as deacons.",
      "originalStructuredText": "Additionally, they must first be tested. Then, if they are above reproach, let them serve as deacons.\n ",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.10"
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.3.11",
      "sourceId": "bsb_usj/1TI.usj#content/38/content/1",
      "sourceLabel": "11",
      "anchors": [
        "1TI.3.11"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "In the same way, the women must be dignified, not slanderers, but temperate and faithful in all things.",
      "originalStructuredText": "In the same way, the women must be dignified, not slanderers, but temperate and faithful in all things.\n ",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.11"
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.3.12",
      "sourceId": "bsb_usj/1TI.usj#content/39/content/1",
      "sourceLabel": "12",
      "anchors": [
        "1TI.3.12"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "A deacon must be the husband of but one wife, a good manager of his children and of his own household.",
      "originalStructuredText": "A deacon must be the husband of but one wife, a good manager of his children and of his own household. ",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.12"
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.3.13",
      "sourceId": "bsb_usj/1TI.usj#content/39/content/3",
      "sourceLabel": "13",
      "anchors": [
        "1TI.3.13"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "For those who have served well as deacons acquire for themselves a high standing and great confidence in the faith that is in Christ Jesus.",
      "originalStructuredText": "For those who have served well as deacons acquire for themselves a high standing and great confidence in the faith that is in Christ Jesus.\n ",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.13"
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.3.14",
      "sourceId": "bsb_usj/1TI.usj#content/41/content/1",
      "sourceLabel": "14",
      "anchors": [
        "1TI.3.14"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things",
      "originalStructuredText": "Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things ",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.14"
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.3.15",
      "sourceId": "bsb_usj/1TI.usj#content/41/content/3",
      "sourceLabel": "15",
      "anchors": [
        "1TI.3.15"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.",
      "originalStructuredText": "in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.\n ",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.15"
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.3.16",
      "sourceId": "bsb_usj/1TI.usj#content/42/content/1",
      "sourceLabel": "16",
      "anchors": [
        "1TI.3.16"
      ],
      "mappingType": "exact",
      "text": "By common confession, the mystery of godliness is great: He appeared in the flesh, was vindicated by the Spirit, was seen by angels, was proclaimed among the nations, was believed in throughout the world, was taken up in glory.",
      "originalStructuredText": "By common confession, the mystery of godliness is great:\n\nHe appeared in the flesh,\nwas vindicated by the Spirit,\nwas seen by angels,\nwas proclaimed among the nations,\nwas believed in throughout the world,\nwas taken up in glory.",
      "sourceRef": "1TI.3.16"
    }
  ],
